The only way to get a sum of 18 is if all three dice show a 6.
The probability of rolling a 6 on one die is $\frac{1}{6}$, so the probability of rolling a 6 on all three dice is $\left(\frac{1}{6}\right)^3 = \boxed{\frac{1}{216}}$.
The answer is: \frac{1}{216}

