solution_steps:
We have
\begin{align*}
f(x) &= \cot \frac{x}{4} - \cot x \\
&= \frac{\cos \frac{x}{4}}{\sin \frac{x}{4}} - \frac{\cos x}{\sin x} \\
&= \frac{\cos \frac{x}{4} \sin x - \cos x \sin \frac{x}{4}}{\sin \frac{x}{4} \sin x} \\
&= \frac{\sin \left( x - \frac{x}{4} \right)}{\sin \frac{x}{4} \sin x} \\
&= \frac{\sin \frac{3x}{4}}{\sin \frac{x}{4} \sin x}.
\end{align*}
Comparing this expression to the given expression, we see that $k = \boxed{\frac{3}{4}}.$
The answer is: \frac{3}{4}

