To multiply two matrices, we multiply corresponding entries in each row of the first matrix by corresponding entries in each column of the second matrix, and then sum the products.
Using this method, we have \[
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 5 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -2 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} (2)(8)+(0)(1) & (2)(-2)+(0)(1) \\ (5)(8)+(-3)(1) & (5)(-2)+(-3)(1) \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 16 & -4 \\ 37 & -13 \end{pmatrix}.
