solution_steps:
Recall that the cross product is distributive, so $\mathbf{a} \times (3 \mathbf{b}) = 3 (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})$.
Using the given information, we have $\mathbf{a} \times (3 \mathbf{b}) = 3 (\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 4 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}) = \begin{pmatrix} 3(5) \\ 3(4) \\ 3(-7) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 15 \\ 12 \\ -21 \end{pmatrix}$.
Thus, the value of $\mathbf{a} \times (3 \mathbf{b})$ is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 15 \\ 12 \\ -21 \end{pmatrix}}$.The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}15\12\-21\end{pmatrix}
